Why EWS End of Life Matters and is Important
Microsoft is retiring the Exchange Web Services (EWS) API.
Starting 1 October 2026, all non-Microsoft apps (like Expert) will be blocked from using EWS with Exchange Online.
Aderant modules must migrate to the Microsoft Graph API – a more secure and modern solution.
What This Means for Your Firm
To remain compatible with Microsoft’s changes, Expert clients will need to apply a new release with support for the Graph API, and redeploy their environment.
This upgrade ensures your firm benefits from the more secure, modern Microsoft Graph API foundation.
Even if you recently upgraded, a new release with support for the Graph API will still be required to keep your system current.
If your firm is planning to implement an affected module, a new release with support for the Graph API will be a necessary prerequisite.
We recognize that additional upgrades are disruptive, which is why our goal is to make this transition as smooth and beneficial as possible - giving your firm both immediate compliance and a stronger long-term platform.
Who is affected by this change?
Not impacted: Expert firms using Expert Classic applications only or Firms with on-premises Exchange servers
Impacted: Firms using Exchange Online (O365) with affected Aderant applications
 
