What is the Timing & Planning
Microsoft’s retirement of EWS takes effect 1 October 2026.
For Expert and Sierra clients, we are pleased to share that version 8.2.4.1, which introduces support for the Graph API, was released in November 2025 and is available. As Microsoft has announced the end of life for EWS, we recognize the importance of ensuring a smooth and timely transition. To support this, we are also actively investigating the possibility of enabling Graph API support in earlier releases for supported versions. We value your partnership and are committed to helping you navigate this change with confidence and minimal disruption.


For CompuLaw: No action is needed now. We will notify your firm when the release is available.
For ATO (Total Office): Firms will need to upgrade to version 9.3, your firm will be notified when this release is available.
For vi by Aderant: On-premises clients must upgrade to 2022 Q1 B1 or later to remain supported. 
What are the Costs & Scope
If your firm is on Expert Sierra, you’re already in great shape! A no cost technical upgrade is available and our Aderant team will be in touch to schedule next steps.
If you are an Expert on-premise client:
A validation SQL script will be available on www.myaderant.com to identify impacted features and define the scope of your upgrade.
Our Professional Services team can assist with the technical upgrade to ensure a smooth transition.
Costs will vary based on your firm’s integrations, customizations, and testing needs; complex environments may require additional scoping.
To avoid scheduling delays, we recommend sharing your validation results early so we can assess your needs and secure your place in the services queue.
We are coordinating with third-party partners to keep the entire ecosystem aligned for a seamless experience.
How do I access the Expert SQL validation script and submit the results?
Note: This step is only needed if your firm is running Expert on-premises. If your firm is on Expert Sierra, CompuLaw, ATO, or vi by Aderant – this step is not required.
For Expert on-premises firms only:
Download the EWS SQL Validation Script from www.myaderant.com (Announcements → or search “Identifying EWS Usage in Expert Systems”) or use this link.
Run the script in your environment.
Submit results for analysis to EWSupgrade@aderant.com.
Receive feedback from Aderant confirming impact and next steps.
